ns and transformers (doc `utility-capex-2027`).\n- Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria.\n- The utility credit note (`utility-credit`) says bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. Norvane priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably, but equity markets have been less receptive. Other nodes are working on whether the plans can be financed, so I haven't judged that here.\n\n**Data centres**\n- Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027 (doc `datacentre-demand`).\n- That is slower than 2026, because power availability limits new sites. Demand is still rising, but at a decelerating rate.\n\n**VLTX exposure** (doc `vltx-order-mix`)\n- Utilities account for 62% of VLTX holdings' orders. Pellham is 35% of utility orders and Norvane is 21%.\n- That puts Pellham at about 22% of total orders and Norvane at about 13%, so roughly 35% of the total rides on those two plans. The utility capex plans therefore matter most for VLTX.\n- The remaining ~38% of orders is not broken down in the documents I found. Data centres are probably part of it, but that is my inference.\n\n**Caveats**\n- I found no order-backlog or actual-orders data, only forward plans and outlooks.\n- Pellham's concentration is a risk: if its capex slips, VLTX demand would be hit disproportionately.","ttft_ms":4835,"type":"result","duration_ms":24291,"uuid":"0796bdac-6e05-4932-b003-50c96fd000d7","ttft_stream_ms":3839,"time_to_request_ms":252,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":9,"system_prompt":23,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":23,"input_attachments":72,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":15,"init_frame_send":10,"engine_pickup":3,"loop_entry":8,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":14,"request_announcements":27,"query_setup":2,"model_gates":2,"tool_schema_build":8,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":2,"request_build":17},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_reque